<Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />

<main>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      {Branding.name()} is an endgame training site. This policy explains what
      information we collect when you use it, why we collect it, and the choices
      you have. It covers the website and every page under it, including the
      guest trainer.
    </p>

    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <p>
      The controller responsible for your personal information is Owen REES, an
      entrepreneur individuel (EI) established in France, trading as {Branding.name()}. Our business register number (SIRET) is
      929&nbsp;553&nbsp;774&nbsp;00019. You can contact us about anything in this
      policy, or about your data, at
      <a href={"mailto:" <> Branding.support_email()}>{Branding.support_email()}</a>
      or <a href="tel:+33683019513">+33 6 83 01 95 13</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account details.</strong>
        If you register, we store your username, email address, and a hashed
        password. We never store passwords in plain text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Training activity.</strong>
        We record the puzzles you attempt and whether you solved them, so we can
        show your progress and keep the daily puzzle meaningful.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Mailing list email.</strong>
        If you join the mailing list — using the form on the home page or the
        checkbox when registering — we store your email address and where you
        signed up, so we can send you occasional updates. You can ask to be
        removed at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical data.</strong>
        We do not keep our own access logs. The companies that host the site
        and run our content delivery network keep short-lived request logs
        (IP address, browser, timestamps) for security, abuse prevention, and
        troubleshooting, under their own retention policies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage data.</strong>
        On public pages and the guest trainer, we use a self-hosted Matomo
        instance to understand aggregate usage. Matomo is configured without
        cookies, with IP addresses shortened before storage, and to respect Do
        Not Track. We do not use user IDs, track signed-in account pages, or
        share this data with third parties.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you send us.</strong>
        If you contact us, we keep the message and our reply for as long as
        needed to help you.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      We use a small number of cookies and local storage entries that are
      required for the site to work:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>a session cookie that keeps you signed in;</li>
      <li>a CSRF token that protects forms from cross-site requests;</li>
      <li>
        a security cookie that our content delivery network, Cloudflare, may set
        when it checks that a request is not automated abuse;
      </li>
      <li>a colour-mode preference stored in your browser.</li>
      <li>
        an analytics opt-out preference stored in your browser's local storage,
        if you choose to opt out.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not use advertising cookies, analytics cookies, or cross-site
      tracking. The only cookie not set by this site is Cloudflare's security
      check described above; our analytics is self-hosted Matomo and is
      configured without cookies. You can clear these entries at any time in
      your browser settings; doing so will sign you out, reset your colour mode,
      and reset your analytics preference.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use a self-hosted Matomo instance at
      <a href="https://analytics.owenrees.eu/">analytics.owenrees.eu</a>
      to understand aggregate use of the public site and guest trainer. It is
      configured without cookies, with IP addresses shortened before storage,
      and to respect Do Not Track. We do not use user IDs, track signed-in
      account pages, or share this data with third parties.
    </p>
    <p>
      Raw analytics data is retained for up to 180 days. We process it on the
      basis of our legitimate interests in improving the service. You can
      object at any time using the control below or by emailing <a href={"mailto:" <> Branding.support_email()}>{Branding.support_email()}</a>.
    </p>
    <p id="analytics-status">Analytics is currently on in this browser.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <button
        id="analytics-opt-out"
        type="button"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-base-content hover:bg-base-200"
      >
        Opt out of analytics
      </button>
      <button
        id="analytics-opt-in"
        type="button"
        hidden
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-base-content hover:bg-base-200"
      >
        Opt back in
      </button>
    </div>

    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To create and secure your account and sign you in.</li>
      <li>To run the trainer and remember your progress.</li>
      <li>To send service emails, such as confirmation and password reset links.</li>
      <li>To send occasional endgame tips and site news, if you opted in.</li>
      <li>
        To understand aggregate use of the public site and guest trainer, and
        improve the service.
      </li>
      <li>To keep the site available, prevent abuse, and fix faults.</li>
      <li>To respond when you ask for help.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We rely on our contract with you to provide the service, our legitimate
      interests in keeping it secure and improving it, and your consent where we
      ask for it. You can withdraw consent at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Guest puzzle limit</h2>
    <p>
      Visitors who use the guest trainer without an account get a limited number
      of free puzzles per UTC day. To enforce that limit and prevent abuse, we
      identify each visitor by a keyed hash (HMAC-SHA256) of their IP address.
      The limiter itself never stores, logs, or shares the raw address.
    </p>
    <p>
      The hash exists only in the memory of the server that handled your request.
      It is tied to the current UTC day, stops being usable at 00:00 UTC, and is
      deleted by a periodic sweep shortly afterwards; it is also discarded when
      the server restarts. It is never written to a database, a log, or a
      backup, and no cookie or other client-side storage is involved. Signed-in
      accounts are not metered this way.
    </p>
    <p>
      We process this hash on the basis of our legitimate interests
      (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR) in keeping the service available and preventing
      abuse of the free tier. We do not share it with anyone. You have the right
      to object to this processing; to do so, contact us using the address below.
    </p>

    <h2 id="hosting-and-infrastructure">Hosting and infrastructure</h2>
    <p>
      The site runs on a virtual private server operated for us by Hetzner
      inside the European Union. Our database runs on the same server, our
      transactional email is sent through Amazon SES in the EU, and our
      self-hosted Matomo analytics runs on infrastructure we control in the EU.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also use Cloudflare as our content delivery network and security proxy.
      Because Cloudflare sits between your browser and our server, it processes
      your IP address, the requested URL, and request headers. Cloudflare is a
      US company, so that request data may be transferred outside the UK and
      EEA. The transfer relies on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and standard
      contractual clauses. Cloudflare and Hetzner each keep their own logs
      under their own retention policies; we do not receive or keep them.
    </p>
    <p>
      These providers act as our processors under data protection law. We share
      with them only what they need to run the service, and we remain
      responsible for how your information is handled.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the
      providers described under
      <a href="#hosting-and-infrastructure">hosting and infrastructure</a>
      — our hosting, content delivery, database, and email delivery providers —
      and only as far as they need it to perform that work. Self-hosted Matomo
      analytics is operated by us on infrastructure we control; we do not share
      that data with third parties. We may also disclose information where the
      law requires it or to protect the rights and safety of our users.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We keep account and training data while your account is open. If you
      delete your account, we remove your personal information within a
      reasonable period, except where we must keep records for legal, security,
      or accounting reasons. We retain raw analytics data for up to 180 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two exceptions are worth naming. If you unsubscribe from the mailing list,
      or ask us not to email you, we keep your address on a suppression list so
      that we do not contact you again; we hold only what is needed to recognise
      the address. We also keep database backups for disaster recovery, stored
      off the primary server, so a deleted account may remain in a backup for
      some time after deletion. We do not use backups to restore individual
      accounts, and we delete them once they are no longer needed.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
      delete, restrict, or export your personal information, and to object to
      some uses of it. You can object to analytics processing at any time using
      the control on this page or by contacting us. To make a request, contact
      us using the address below. If you are in the UK or EU and are unhappy
      with our response, you can complain to your local data protection
      authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the service changes. When we do, we will
      change the date at the top of this page and, for significant changes,
      notify signed-in users by email or on the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data can be sent to <a href={"mailto:" <> Branding.support_email()}>{Branding.support_email()}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</main>
